# Everything the image does not need. The Dockerfile's COPY lines name what they
# want, so this is defence in depth plus a smaller build context.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
PLANS
README.md
DESIGN.md
parsed-rules-aug-2026.md
prolog/test
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.log
httpd.log

# The UI toolchain. web/app.css, web/map.js, web/rtw.pvm and web/vendor/ are all
# generated and committed, so the image carries the outputs and never needs the
# inputs, the compilers, or node. Two things are NOT excluded, on purpose:
# web/fonts/NOTICE.md and OFL.txt, because the licence requires them to travel
# with the fonts, and web/vendor/, because the page loads the Prolog engine from
# there.
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
.impeccable.md
web/app.src.css
web/map.src.js
web/check-contrast.mjs
web/rtw.build.json

# The raw earning-table captures are input for the generators, not for the
# validator. What gets loaded is the .pl files built from them, and those are
# committed alongside. See prolog/data/earn/sources/README.md.
prolog/data/earn/sources
